      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-297686",
      ":question/problem": "Two departments in a company, each with $9$ employees, reported their annual salaries. The mean salary for Department A is $$54,000$, while the mean salary for Department B is $$59,110$.\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\n1. Every employee in Department B earns more than every employee in Department A.\n2. There is at least one employee in Department B who earns more than at least one employee in Department A.\n3. The median salary in Department B is greater than the median salary in Department A."
