      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-297728",
      ":question/problem": "Two groups of office workers, each with $9$ members, tracked their daily caffeine intake. The mean intake for Group A is $185.56$ mg, while the mean for Group B is $140$ mg.\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\n1. Every member of Group A consumed more caffeine than every member of Group B.\n2. The median caffeine intake in Group A is greater than the median in Group B.\n3. There is at least one member of Group B who consumed less caffeine than at least one member of Group A."
    }
